# Shell scripts MUST be stored and checked out with LF.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and run on Linux. A .sh file committed with CRLF fails on a
# GitHub runner with `$'\r': command not found` -- an error that names a byte nobody can see and
# points at the wrong line. scripts/check-db-url.sh is run by the migrate job, so it would break
# the one step whose job is explaining breakage.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by Linux tooling.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
